WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.519 --> 00:00:03.102
(gentle music)

00:00:21.447 --> 00:00:23.600
- I think that he will probably be

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:26.311
further ahead in this exercise than I am

00:00:26.311 --> 00:00:28.261
when it comes to questions about myself.

00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:29.589
- I'm interested to see what she does

00:00:29.589 --> 00:00:32.589
'cause she's a pretty humble person.

00:00:35.056 --> 00:00:37.645
- [Host] Take a step
forward if you trust Hailee

00:00:37.645 --> 00:00:39.228
to do your laundry.

00:00:42.536 --> 00:00:45.570
Take a step forward if you
wouldn't change anything

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:46.987
on Hailee's face.

00:00:47.914 --> 00:00:50.447
Step forward if you wish Hailee could see

00:00:50.447 --> 00:00:52.280
how beautiful she was.

00:00:57.145 --> 00:01:01.627
Take a step forward if
Isabel gives good advice.

00:01:01.627 --> 00:01:04.199
Take a step forward if you think Isabel

00:01:04.199 --> 00:01:05.949
has a beautiful body.

00:01:09.848 --> 00:01:12.467
Take a step forward if you wish Isabel

00:01:12.467 --> 00:01:15.134
could see how beautiful she was.

00:01:17.201 --> 00:01:20.951
Take a step forward if
Vicky makes you laugh.

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:25.932
Take a step forward if you think Vicky

00:01:25.932 --> 00:01:27.515
lights up the room.

00:01:29.054 --> 00:01:32.721
Take a step forward if
you believe in Vicky.

00:01:36.037 --> 00:01:39.979
Take a step forward if
Cesar gives good advice.

00:01:39.979 --> 00:01:42.216
Take a step back if you wish Cesar

00:01:42.216 --> 00:01:45.133
was capable of achieving his goals.

00:01:46.737 --> 00:01:50.404
Take a step forward if
you believe in Cesar.

00:01:54.114 --> 00:01:56.531
(soft piano)

00:02:04.108 --> 00:02:05.914
- It should be okay, I
should just be able to like

00:02:05.914 --> 00:02:08.030
walk forward if that's how I truly feel,

00:02:08.030 --> 00:02:10.426
but there's a moment of
hesitation and then I just like,

00:02:10.426 --> 00:02:11.343
don't move.

00:02:13.601 --> 00:02:16.662
I think it's sort of
symptomatic of being in a

00:02:16.662 --> 00:02:19.398
loving relationship where
you need that other person

00:02:19.398 --> 00:02:20.648
to support you.

00:02:25.352 --> 00:02:26.869
- I'm real, you know.

00:02:26.869 --> 00:02:28.286
- [Isabel] Cesar.

00:02:29.353 --> 00:02:32.764
- I thought I'd be more
confident, but it's just,

00:02:32.764 --> 00:02:34.961
I guess the honesty
just came out, I guess.

00:02:34.961 --> 00:02:36.397
I was being honest with myself.

00:02:36.397 --> 00:02:37.744
Thank you for believing in me.

00:02:37.744 --> 00:02:39.577
- Awe, of course I do.

00:02:42.422 --> 00:02:43.567
- It's fair, right?

00:02:43.567 --> 00:02:44.633
(laughing)

00:02:44.633 --> 00:02:45.539
I don't know.

00:02:45.539 --> 00:02:47.964
- I think it falls in line
with what I said earlier

00:02:47.964 --> 00:02:50.668
about how I'm just, I'm
really hard on myself

00:02:50.668 --> 00:02:52.917
all the time and I know that.

00:02:52.917 --> 00:02:55.275
- To me, she's perfect in my eyes.

00:02:55.275 --> 00:02:57.003
There's little things here
and there where you're like,

00:02:57.003 --> 00:02:58.642
does she make silly
decisions where it's like,

00:02:58.642 --> 00:03:02.225
I don't necessarily
see that as a negative.

00:03:03.276 --> 00:03:05.693
(soft music)

